Package: qadam-flow-common
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Breaks: qadam-flow (<< 1.1.0~stable.b1)
Description: qadam-flow shared runtime tree (Node.js modules, builds)
 Shared program tree for the qadam-flow master and worker binary packages:
 the vendored node_modules, the built engine / API / web / qadam dists, the
 bundled qadam catalogue manifests and the workspace manifests under
 /usr/lib/qadam-flow. The web frontend lives under /usr/share/qadam-flow/web
 and the isolate sandbox configuration under /usr/local/etc/isolate.
 .
 Running the daemon itself requires either qadam-flow (the master, with the
 PostgreSQL 18 + pgvector database and Redis) or qadam-flow-worker (stateless
 execution node that talks to a master over HTTP).

Package: qadam-flow
Architecture: all
Depends:
 qadam-flow-common (= ${source:Version}),
 nodejs (>= 24.21),
 postgresql-18-pgvector (>= 0.8.7) | postgresql-17-pgvector,
 redis-server (>= 7.0) | valkey,
 adduser,
 openssl,
 ${misc:Depends},
Recommends: nginx
Description: master service of the qadam-flow platform (API, frontend, scheduler)
 Master service of Qadam Flow, the AI-first workflow automation platform.
 Runs as the systemd unit qadam-flow-master.service on port 3000 (unified
 behind a reverse proxy on 80/443 with the recommended nginx), owns the
 PostgreSQL 18 + pgvector database and the Redis/Valkey queue, and serves
 the web frontend from /usr/share/qadam-flow/web. Runtime user: qadam.
 .
 Package layout follows the Docker image: the program tree lives in
 /usr/lib/qadam-flow, cache in /var/cache/qadam-flow (systemd
 CacheDirectory), qadam version store in /var/lib/qadam-flow/qadam-versions
 (systemd StateDirectory subdirectory).

Package: qadam-flow-worker
Architecture: all
Depends:
 qadam-flow-common (= ${source:Version}),
 nodejs (>= 24.21),
 adduser,
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: qadam-flow worker (flow execution node)
 Stateless execution service of Qadam Flow. Runs as the systemd unit
 qadam-flow-worker.service on port 3001 (health server only), polls the
 master over HTTP (AP_WORKER_API_URL, default 127.0.0.1:3000) and runs flow
 steps with its own engine processes. Deliberately does NOT depend on
 PostgreSQL or Redis: only the master talks to the database and the queue,
 which is what makes this package installable on separate hosts.
 .
 Security defaults run in UNSANDBOXED/SANDBOX_CODE_ONLY mode. The
 SANDBOX_PROCESS and SANDBOX_CODE_AND_PROCESS modes additionally need the
 isolate sandbox bridge (/usr/src/node_modules symlink, provided by
 qadam-flow-common) plus unit hardening; see
 /usr/share/doc/qadam-flow-common/README.Debian.
